Heavy Periods and Long Commutes: How to Stay Leak-Ready

Long commutes can be stressful enough without worrying about your period. If you experience heavy menstrual flow, spending hours in traffic, buses, trains, or cabs can make period management more challenging.

Fortunately, a little preparation can go a long way.

Why Are Long Commutes Challenging During Heavy Flow?

During a long commute, you may not have immediate access to a clean washroom. You may also spend extended periods sitting, which can make you more conscious of leakage.

Create a Commute-Friendly Period Kit

Keep a small pouch containing:

Several sanitary pads
Tissues
Spare underwear
Disposal bags
Hand sanitiser
An extra clothing item if needed

Keep the pouch somewhere easily accessible.

Choose Appropriate Menstrual Protection

If your flow is heavy, consider a sanitary pad that provides suitable absorbency and coverage.

